    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2D4kQX5Tmjr48sWCkaDNynw)_\n\n**Before:** no way to turn loose thesis ideas into tasks from Emacs.\n\n**After:** `M-x sp-thesis-dump` opens a buffer for a brain dump. `C-c C-c` sends it to Claude, which returns annotated Org `TODO` tasks (summary, tags, effort, citekeys), a checklist of citekeys to look up (checked by Emacs against the `.bib` files, so \"missing\" does not depend on what Claude says) and open questions. The answer opens in a review buffer; `C-c C-c` files it under a heading of the task file (created if missing).\n\n**Portable:** `sp-thesis-dump.el` needs only Emacs 28.1, Org 9.5 and the `claude` command. Project variables (task file, heading, bib files, TODO keywords, tags, citation style, citekey style, outline file, language) are prompted for when missing and can be saved in the project's `.dir-locals.el`; `C-u M-x sp-thesis-dump` asks for all again. Machine settings (the `claude` command, `--mcp-config`, `--allowedTools`) are global and never read from `.dir-locals.el`. Copy the one file into the thesis repo's Emacs setup.\n\n**How \"org-mcp\" is used:** MCP puts the model in the client role, so Emacs cannot send to Claude through an MCP server. Emacs runs `claude -p` in the project directory, and if `sp-thesis-dump-claude-allowed-tools` lists the org-mcp tools, Claude can read the Org files for context. Emacs does the filing. Without MCP the prompt carries the existing headlines, known citekeys and an optional outline file.\n\n**Also:** literate doc `docs/tangles/custom/sp-thesis-dump.org` (tangles the module and a companion Claude Code skill `docs/skills/thesis-brain-dump/SKILL.md` for the same job outside Emacs), `init.el` loads it after `sp-sandbox`, entries in `docs/main.org` and `CHANGELOG.org`.\n\n**Tested:** byte-compiles without warnings on Emacs 29.3; settings, prompting and saving to `.dir-locals.el`, prompt, parsing (including a code fence), rendering, filing under a nested heading and the failure path were run in batch Emacs against a stand-in `claude` script.\n\n**Not tested:** the real `claude -p --output-format json` envelope, reading the prompt from stdin, `--mcp-config`/`--allowedTools`, the org-mcp tool names, the GUI on macOS, and the skill.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eik89TBj6BVLrQsY7wFL2E)_",
